{
  "note": "Synthetic Kuaishou feed answers (docs/modules/M5.5-kuaishou.md). An answer is `payload` JSON-encoded `layers` times (default 2, as the recorded feed: a JSON string holding the JSON object), or the literal body text `raw`. `feeds` are decoded one by one as the client gets them (the body decoded once, as dio did for a JSON content type, then 3.x parseFeedPayload). `sessions` replay one connection: each step answers one HTTP request in order (`error`: no response; `status`: that status; otherwise the answer with status 200); when the steps run out the next request never completes and the session ends. A feed with `skipEntry` is also decoded by 3.x without that entry of `liveStreamFeeds` (`v3WithoutEntry`): the new code skips an entry it cannot read, where 3.x failed the whole answer. All user ids, names and texts are made up.",
